diff -Naur a/debian/changelog b/debian/changelog
--- a/debian/changelog	2026-06-25 11:47:11.000000000 -0500
+++ b/debian/changelog	2026-07-10 14:46:08.750601655 -0500
@@ -1,3 +1,25 @@
+nfs-ganesha (9.13-1+klldap1) unstable; urgency=medium
+
+  * nfs-klldap-host Phase 2 uplift build; 9.13 source, flag-only delta
+    (see nfs-klldap-host-ganesha-refactor-plan.md sections 2.1 and the
+    2026-07-10 Realignment).
+  * Disable MSPAC support (_MSPAC_SUPPORT=NO): un-stubs the principal-based
+    group resolution path in uid2grp (uid2grp.c returns NULL for every
+    principal when MSPAC is compiled in) and removes the wbclient/winbind
+    dependency. Carried over from the 9.6+klldap1 Phase 1 build.
+  * Trim FSALs to VFS only: disable CEPH, RGW, GLUSTER, GPFS, PROXY_V4,
+    NULL, MEM, RADOS recovery/URLs and 9P; drop the per-FSAL binary
+    packages and their build dependencies (libcephfs-dev, libglusterfs-dev,
+    librados-dev, librgw-dev, libwbclient-dev). Carried over from Phase 1.
+  * Keep stock ENABLE_VFS_POSIX_ACL=YES (Phase 1 had removed it): Phase 2
+    ships one ACL-capable binary; NOACL shares are enforced per-export via
+    Disable_ACL. ENABLE_VFS_DEBUG_ACL stays off (in-memory store, not
+    suitable for persistent ACLs).
+  * Retained unchanged: GSS, DBus, nfsidmap, admin tools, monitoring,
+    man pages, system ntirpc linkage, source version 9.13.
+
+ -- Aelieth <shaiaelieth@gmail.com>  Fri, 10 Jul 2026 00:00:00 +0000
+
 nfs-ganesha (9.13-1) unstable; urgency=medium
 
   * New upstream version 9.13
