 #!/usr/bin/make -f
 # -*- makefile -*-
 #
+# nfs-klldap-host Phase 2 uplift build (refactor plan 2.1, realigned
+# 2026-07-10). Delta from stock 9.13-1 rules:
+#   - _MSPAC_SUPPORT=NO (restores uid2grp principal path, drops wbclient)
+#   - FSALs trimmed to VFS only (CEPH/RGW/GLUSTER/GPFS/PROXY/NULL/MEM off,
+#     RADOS recovery+URLs off, 9P off; arch-conditional blocks removed)
+#   - LIZARDFS/SAUNAFS pinned NO (stock left them to auto-disable on
+#     missing libs; pinned for determinism)
+#   - install steps for removed FSAL sample configs dropped
+# ENABLE_VFS_POSIX_ACL=YES is stock and deliberately retained: Phase 2
+# ships ONE ACL-capable binary; NOACL shares are enforced per-export via
+# Disable_ACL (the debug-ACL store was ruled out — in-memory only).
+# Everything else (ntirpc linkage, monitoring, admin tools, DBus, man
+# pages, hardening) is unchanged from stock.
+#
 # Expected debian/rules file that is used by the dpkg build procedure
 #
 #   $ git clone <nfs-ganesha>
